# kk: NaN constants keep their sign and payload
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46119 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->


kk: NaN constants keep their sign and payload

Before, every NaN constant was written as NAN (0x7fc00000) and the sign
or payload was lost. For example, 0xffc00000 came out as 0x7fc00000.

The idea is that now NaN is written with its exact bits.

Assisted-by: LLM
Original Language: ESP
